<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imad al-Din Abu Bakr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Imad al-Din Abu Bakr was a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artuqid-dynasty">Artuqid dynasty</a> who established a separate Artuqid line at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harput">Harput</a> in 1185, breaking away from the Artuqids of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasankeyf">Hasankeyf</a>. His small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> ruled the Harput region until it was annexed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> in 1234.</p></div>
